From 1c464225f40e1831132d742eebf39e433f9fc51d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arslan8 <arslankhan52@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:53:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] SITL: CP Models vehicle FMU as in-process physics (prototype)

--model cpvehicle:<descriptor> loads a CP Models (ModelicaCPSLibrary)
vehicle FMU into the SITL process through the CP Models vehicle runtime
and uses it in place of SITL's built-in vehicle physics.

- SIM_CPVehicle: servo outputs drive pwm_actuation_v1 (identity or
  CPV_CHANNEL_MAP); kinematic_state_v1 truth and imu_v1 specific force
  fill position, velocity, attitude, body rate and accel_body; SITL's
  home becomes the FMU's geodetic origin; the FMU is advanced to SITL's
  frame time in integer microseconds; any runtime error panics instead
  of continuing on stale physics.
- waf: --cpvehicle=PATH links the runtime; without it the model is
  compiled out.
- examples/CPVehicle: parameters matching the CP Models quad and a
  checked guided mission.

Tested with ArduCopter 4.6.2 and the CP Models quad only.
