--- /dev/null
+++ b/libraries/SITL/examples/CPVehicle/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@
+# CP Models vehicle FMU as SITL physics (prototype)
+
+`--model cpvehicle:<descriptor>` replaces SITL's built-in vehicle physics
+with a CP Models (ModelicaCPSLibrary) vehicle FMU, loaded **into the SITL
+process** through the CP Models vehicle runtime (`libcpvehicle`). The
+autopilot and SITL's sensor simulation are unchanged. There is no socket and
+no second process (compare `libraries/SITL/examples/JSON`).
+
+Status: prototype, tested only with ArduCopter 4.6.2 and the CP Models quad
+(`configs/quad.toml`). It is not upstream ArduPilot code.
+
+## Build
+
+```sh
+# CP Models: build the FMU, write its descriptor, build the runtime
+cd ModelicaCPSLibrary
+python3 tools/vehicle_interface/build_vehicle_fmu.py configs/quad.toml build/quad.fmu
+(cd tools/vehicle_interface && python3 -m cp_vehicle_interface prepare ../../build/quad.fmu \
+    ../../build/quad --require pwm_actuation_v1 --require kinematic_state_v1 --require imu_v1)
+cmake -S runtime -B build/runtime-release -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF
+cmake --build build/runtime-release
+
+# ArduPilot (a venv with future, empy==3.3.4, pexpect, dronecan, pymavlink on PATH)
+./waf configure --board sitl --cpvehicle=/path/to/ModelicaCPSLibrary
+./waf copter
+```
+
+Without `--cpvehicle` nothing changes: the model is compiled out
+(`AP_SIM_CPVEHICLE_ENABLED`).
+
+## Run
+
+```sh
+build/sitl/bin/arducopter --model cpvehicle:/path/to/ModelicaCPSLibrary/build/quad/vehicle.json \
+    --defaults Tools/autotest/default_params/copter.parm,libraries/SITL/examples/CPVehicle/cpvehicle_quad.parm \
+    --home 40.414929,-86.932387,149,0 --speedup 4 -I3
+libraries/SITL/examples/CPVehicle/fly_mission.py --connect tcp:127.0.0.1:5790
+```
+
+`fly_mission.py` waits for the EKF to use GPS, then arms in GUIDED, takes off
+to 5 m, holds, flies 20 m north and back, lands, and checks each step.
+
+## What the adapter does (`SIM_CPVehicle.cpp`)
+
+| SITL | From the FMU (vehicle interface v1) |
+|---|---|
+| servo outputs `SERVO1..n` | `pwm_actuation_v1`: servo *k* drives `pwm[k+1]`, or `CPV_CHANNEL_MAP` (one SITL servo index per FMU element). A zero output leaves the channel at its previous value. |
+| `position`, `velocity_ef`, `dcm`, `gyro` | `kinematic_state_v1`: CG truth, NED, scalar-first quaternion |
+| `accel_body` | `imu_v1` `accel` (specific force, FRD) |
+| home | sets the FMU's geodetic origin (`lat0`, `lon0`, `ground_alt_wgs84`) before initialization. SITL has no geoid, so home altitude is used as the ellipsoid altitude. |
+| time | the FMU is advanced to SITL's `time_now_us + frame_time_us` (integer µs from start) every frame, in steps of at most 2 ms |
+
+- **Sensors.** SITL simulates GPS, compass, barometer and IMU noise from that
+  truth, as it does for every model. The FMU's own GPS, magnetometer and
+  barometer outputs are not used. Use a model with an ideal IMU so IMU noise
+  is not applied twice.
+- **Not modelled by the FMU here.** Battery voltage is a constant
+  `SIM_BATT_VOLTAGE`. Wind (`SIM_WIND_*`) is ignored and reported at start.
+  Payloads and clamps are not supported.
+- **Failures.** Any runtime error stops SITL (`AP_HAL::panic`) with the
+  reason. It never continues on stale physics.
+- **Channel order.** `configs/quad.toml` is wired in ArduCopter's Quad-X order
+  (`actuatorIndex = [3, 2, 4, 1]`), so the identity map is right. The hexa
+  composition is not in ArduCopter's Hexa-X order; it needs a
+  `CPV_CHANNEL_MAP` and has not been flown here.
+
+## Measured (ArduCopter 4.6.2, CP Models quad, `--speedup 4`)
+
+Two launches in the same directory (the second reuses the saved parameters)
+both passed: hover at 4.99 m with drift ≤ 0.01 m, the 20 m north waypoint
+reached to within 0.4 m, landed 0.25–0.28 m from home, maximum tilt 17.5°.
+
+## Differences from FastDyn (QEMU)
+
+| | FastDyn | This prototype |
+|---|---|---|
+| Autopilot | firmware binary on an emulated board | native SITL build |
+| Sensors | FMU sensor outputs through emulated drivers | SITL sensor simulation from FMU truth |
+| Clock | QEMU instruction count, 1 ms board tick | SITL frame loop (default 1200 Hz) |
+| FMU steps | ≤ 2 ms per step at each timer tick | one step per SITL frame (≈ 0.83 ms) |
diff --git a/libraries/SITL/examples/CPVehicle/cpvehicle_quad.parm b/libraries/SITL/examples/CPVehicle/cpvehicle_quad.parm
